 her  own family and going to jail for the  rest of her life so the best course of  action for her is to pin this on jon  another thread which had no significance  to the actual ending but could be woven  into this new  ending is silvia's relationship with  prosecuting attorney  katherine stamper they used to intern  together for a bit when they first  started off as lawyers but this  connection never really pays off in the  show she waves to her when entering the  court and there's another meaningless  scene with them in the washroom but if  sylvia actually killed elena  catherine would be a powerful ally to  have when you're the actual murderer so  i guess this all comes down to how  sylvia would be caught and i think the  best way to do this would be through  haley fitzgerald  bringing sylvia to the stand haley has  said multiple times throughout the  season  that she'll be able to find anything out  i will find  out hell she was able to hack into all  the jurors facebooks and manipulate the  advertisements they were fed what if she  secretly knew something about sylvia  couldn't 100 prove it but had to use her  wits to get a confession out of her  while on the stand we've already seen  how haley can amp  up the pressure and elicit huge  reactions from those she questions  like what happened to fernando i'd  equate this scene to that famous one in  a few good men where tom cruise's  character slowly applies pressure until  jack nicholson snaps you can't handle  the truth  this could also be juxtaposed with  flashbacks of sylvia committing the  murder  kind of like how we saw jon commit it in  the real version it would also be a big  reveal for grace  john and everyone else in the courtroom  leading me to believe it would be a more  satisfying and rewarding ending than the  haphazard chase scene we got there's  even room to see what would happen to  these characters after the trial and  allow us to decompress  all in all this is just what i came up  with in a little bit of time so there  are probably lots of better options and  ways to go about ending the show i even  thought about covering the grandfather  as the potential killer as there are  almost  just as many hidden clues that point to  him as well but i want to hear what you  thought of the ending am i completely  wrong here or would you have liked to  have seen something different  make sure to leave a comment below  thanks for watching everyone make sure  to like subscribe and share and for more  bad takes you can always follow me on  twitter and instagram  at thingstoryt until next time remember  daddy loves you very much  you
 

